module Core

### Represents the aggregate protocol for integer-like numeric types.
### `Integral` combines exact arithmetic, floor division, exponentiation,
### bitwise operations, and shifting into the standard surface expected from
### signed and unsigned integer families.
protocol Integral obeys Addable, Subtractable, Multiplicable, FloorDivisible, Exponentiable, Bitwiseable, Shiftable
  ### Renders this value in base `radix` (2 to 36), digits past 9 as lowercase letters, with a leading
  ### `-` when negative. Crashes on any other radix. `hex()` / `bin()` / `oct()` are shorthands for it.
  ### :param radix: The numeric base.
  ### :returns: The rendered `Text`.
  @readonly
  routine Me.to_text(radix: S32) -> Text
